Subject: [PATCH] net: SOCKS5 datagram socket over UDP ASSOCIATE

Adds SOCKS5DatagramClientSocket, a datagram socket that relays through a
SOCKS5 proxy with RFC 1928 UDP ASSOCIATE. It holds the TCP control
connection open for the life of the association and sends nothing on it
after the handshake. Name destinations go to the proxy for resolution,
so HTTP/3 through the proxy makes no local DNS query for the
destination. Nothing uses the socket until patch 0080 wires it into
QUIC.

